Z||000004||BOILERMAKER||05-31-99||07:35 PM||||I am also getting ready to change mine to R134, but I need all of the parts.  The only thing that I have right now is the R134 and the tools to put it in with.  Can someone help me to find the material I will need (approx. costs would be appreciated).  This will entail a complete restoration I believe.  I can find old equipment, but doesn't the R134 have to be run at higher pressure.  If this is true, I don't know if I should trust my old equipment with the higher pressure.  Any thoughts?
Z||000005||Phil||06-01-99||04:46 AM||||The parts you need depend on why your old system wasn't working, new refrig. wont cure a broken system.
Z||000006||BOILERMAKER||06-01-99||06:45 AM||||I don't want to pay $40+ per pound of refrig.  That is why I want to change to R134.  I want to make the change now while my engine is out.  I only have a week or so before the engine is going back in, so information would be appreciated.<p>I need new equipment if the new pressure that the R134 runs at might be questionable for the old factory compressor/hoses/etc...
Z||000007||theogre||06-01-99||07:47 AM||||at the very least. you must replace the acc/dryer, orifice tube, hose O rings and compressor. All hoses should be pressure tested. The entire system should be presure tested before loading the 134. These tests should be done by a trained tech. they are signifigantly dangerous.<p>you maybe can get away without replacement of the compressor, but it's very likely that the main seal in it is already leaking, or will very soon.
Z||000008||BOILERMAKER||06-02-99||07:07 AM||||OK, I am a lot more understanding of what I have to do now.  Couple more questions and I should be done.  Where would I get the hoses for the AC system?  I want to make sure new hoses are being put in on this job.  Also, I am guessing that Autozone or Pep-Boys would have all O-rings and ACC/Dryer??
Z||000009||theogre||06-02-99||07:33 AM||||some hoses are no longer available thru GM. You may have to have these fabricated.<p>The acc/dryer and allot of the rest is standard GM parts and are available every where.
